\noindent \textbf{Evaluation Metrics.}
We evaluate the framework from three perspectives: concept consistency, diagnostic performance, and report quality. 
Concept Accuracy/F1 measures the agreement between clinically predefined attributes extracted from the generated report and the ground-truth structured annotations. 
Concept Accuracy is computed as the average categorical accuracy across all supervised attributes, and Concept F1 reflects balanced precision and recall at the attribute level. 
Diagnosis Accuracy (ACC) evaluates the correctness of the final prediction. 
Report Generation Metrics include BLEU-4 and ROUGE-L, which quantify n-gram overlap between generated reports and reference reports.
